about 8 percent of clark county  residents are fully vaccinated this  according to the department of health  and human  services while we are beginning week 13  of the state's vaccination  efforts the i-team's vanessa murphy has  some basics  on what nevadans need to know she is  live in the digital center with more  vanessa brian some misinformation has  been trickling in and we want to provide  some clarification for  our viewers now one reminder is no one  should be paying  any out of pocket costs for the covid 19  vaccine if someone calls you  asking for payment information do not  provide it  the state has warned nevadans before  scammers are trying to take advantage of  people during the pandemic  according to candice mcdaniel who heads  the state's vaccination efforts even if  your health insurance information is  collected at a vaccination site  you still should not pay any  out-of-pocket costs  the insurance might be billed for an  administrative fee like through a  pharmacy as an example  but there is no out of out of pocket  cost whatsoever  another concern we've heard is the issue  of identification  and whether you need a nevada id like a  driver's license  to get vaccinated here mcdaniel tells me  an individual would not be turned away  if they do not have a nevada id  you will need to present id at the  vaccination site  so the dose can be reported but there is  no requirement  that it has to be from nevada and we  have more information about  booking appointments other issues at  eight newsnow dot com nevada 211 is also  a resource we have that information here  up on the web  but of course you can call 2-1-1 they  can help you book an appointment it's a  great resource  for anyone having trouble doing that  online or who may not have  internet access again that's nevada211  reporting live vanessa murphy 8 news now
 

